# REGENT OF ENREKANG SOUTH SULAWESI PROVINCE

# REGIONAL REGULATION OF ENREKANG REGENCY NUMBER 1 OF 2018

# CONCERNING PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

# BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

# REGENT OF ENREKANG.

Considering:  
a. that in order to guarantee and protect the rights of women and children so that they can participate optimally in accordance with human dignity and honor, and receive protection from violence, it is necessary to undertake efforts to protect women and children;  
b. that violence against women and children in Enrekang Regency continues to increase and spread, causing community members to be unsafe in carrying out their lives, so that integrated protection efforts are needed;  
c. that based on the provisions in Article 12 of Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government, women's empowerment and child protection are mandatory governmental affairs for regional governments;  
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women and Children;

In View of:  
1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia; 2. Law Number 29 of 1959 concerning Establishment of Level II Regions in Sulawesi (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1959 Number 74, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1822);

3. Law Number 1 of 1974 concerning Marriage (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1974 Number 1, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3019);  
4. Law Number 4 of 1979 concerning Child Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1979 Number 32, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3143);  
5. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);  
6. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);  
7. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606);  
8. Law Number 13 of 2003 concerning Manpower (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 39, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4279);  
9. Law Number 20 of 2003 concerning National Education System (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 78, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4301);  
10. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);  
11. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);  
12. Law Number 36 of 2009 concerning Health (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2009 Number 144, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5063);  
13. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times, most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);  
14. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);  
15. Presidential Regulation Number 18 of 2014 concerning Protection of Women and Children in Social Conflict (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 44);

Regulation of the Minister of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 6 of 2015 concerning System for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 615); 2018 S32 With Mutual Approval  REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF ENREKANG REGENCY  and

# REGENT OF ENREKANG

# DECIDES:

To Establish: REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN.

